sec.p:
NK cell cytotoxic function was assessed by the measuring the number of live cells identified by calcein-AM (CAM) labeling. Target cells and NK cells were labelled with CAM (BD Pharmingen) and calcein-violet (CV) (eBioscience), respectively. NK cells were co-cultured with target cells at the indicated ratios for 4 hours in triplicate, and the samples were analyzed by flow cytometry (Attune NXT, Invitrogen) in 96 well plates. The CV-positive NK cells were gated out for analysis. Percent cell lysis was calculated as follows:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
